# Distribution for CommonsLang_Rust (Windows_x86_64)

Builds the Rust toolchain objects for the `Windows_x86_64` slot and proves them by building a
static library that uses ring's C and assembly.

## rustc, cargo and the host standard library

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Host.Files@1.99.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/host-Windows_x86_64 slot=Release.Windows_x86_64
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "od5zkkbxsqzilvrtpn3osxvbnj5ewytnjkzi4527ls3462em2vdaq")\;

## The standard library for the target

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Std.Files@1.99.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/std slot=Release.Windows_x86_64
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "oll6wadmeaql6dca57juba3xdikbmpazeoddwfud6rmstm7ucht4q")\;

## The CargoLock dialog (author time)

Ships the `CommonsLang_Rust.CargoLock.Bundle` dialog, which writes a crates bundle from a
`Cargo.lock`.

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.CargoLock.Export@1.0.0 -f ${RUNTIME}/CargoLock.Export.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "o6sto7llzlwf4l7zdmwsapqjwsn2mrdchtyumnyyzvefq2hptjyvq")\;

## Usage: a static library that uses ring

`assets/fixture/ring` is a Cargo workspace whose `ringlib` crate calls ring's SHA-256.
Its crates bundle came from the CargoLock dialog. cargo builds it offline.

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Cargo.F_StaticLib@1.0.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/ringlib
  >   modver=CommonsLang_Rust.Fixture.RingLib@1.0.0
  >   srcasset=CommonsLang_Rust.Apparatus.RingFixture@1.0.1 srcpath=assets/fixture/ring
  >   crates=CommonsLang_Rust.Fixture.Crates.Bundle@1.0.0 package=ringlib
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "op37o4wpblrxi5oerfvz6exdvsoy3od6hfpy7fpooe3s3qsvfctxa")\;
